Plan C (AgentX): ISS owns ifTable, so SNMP/AgentX SET ifAdminStatus lands in ISS (`cfa2/src/ifmibwr.c:IfAdminStatusSet`), NOT the net-snmp ies-auto-mibs Flask path (change A skipped ifmibdb). Two things came out of wiring SET→config and observing load behaviour (2026-06-25, branch `snmp-agentx-default-agentx`).

**Q2 — SET ifAdminStatus → config layer (DONE, +21/-2 in ifmibwr.c).** The framework's real SET URI fn is `LibFrameworkUri_PatchUri(handle, uri, token, json, &ret)` (lib `lib_moxa_framework_uri`, in-process HTTP PATCH to 127.0.0.1:80 nginx → config_layer; NOT a shell — `/sbin/ies_uri_handle_client` is the shell variant; `ies_uri_handle_oid_update` is a *different* mechanism = socket IPC to the urihook daemon). Token (`gUriToken`/`security_tokens[]`) is per-SNMPv3-user, minted by `LibUtil_CreateToken(user, service, file)` (`lib_moxa_utility`); AgentX does NOT forward securityName to the subagent, so ISS can't get the per-user token. BUT no need to build any of this: **ISS already wraps it** — `PortSetAdminStatus2MxCfg(ifIndex, adminStatus)` and `PortSetAdminStatus2MxCfgAsync(...)` in `future/mxcfg/src/portmxcfg.c` do token+handle+GET-modify-PATCH (`gMxCfgToken` auto-minted by mxcfg), already used by TurboRing/TurboChain/loop-protection(lpapi)/port-security/RLPS/goosecheck. Fix = one call in `IfAdminStatusSet` after `nmhSetIfAdminStatus` succeeds: `PortSetAdminStatus2MxCfgAsync(ifIndex, value)` (declared via `extern` to avoid mxcfg include-path). Async (detached thread) so the single SNMP/AgentX task isn't blocked on the HTTP round-trip. ifAdminStatus up(1)/down(2)==CFA_IF_UP/DOWN, pass through. CAVEAT: `PortSetAdminStatus2MxCfg` handles PHYSICAL PORTS only (portTable, URI built as ifIndex-1). port-channel / L3-VLAN ifIndex need the other URI shapes from `ies-auto-mibs/.../uHandle_ifmib_ifTable_ifAdminStatus`: `/api/v1/setting/data/laSettings/portChannelTable/<idx>/enable` and `/ipInterface/l3VlanIfTable/<idx>/adminStatusUpEnable` (physical port = `/ifmib/portTable/<port-1>/enable`, body bool true/false). Fire-and-forget: PATCH failure not reported to SNMP SET result.

**Q1 — AgentX session drops under rapid/bursty requests; only disable/enable snmpsubagent recovers.** Root cause = TCP stream framing treated as datagram (NOT mem-pool exhaustion, which only drops packets and self-recovers). `snxtrans.c:SnxTransTcpRcvPacket` does a single `recv(sock, buf, SNX_MAX_MTU)` and treats it as one message; `SnxMainProcessRcvdPkt`'s `SNX_MUL_REQ_PKT` loop handles multiple WHOLE PDUs but discards a partial trailing PDU → inbound stream desyncs. `snxtrans.c:SnxTransTcpTxPacket` only checks `send()<0`, so a partial write (`0<ret<len`, common under master backpressure) is treated as success → outbound stream truncated → master closes session. Fresh socket (disable→enable, `SnxTransDeInit`) re-aligns the byte stream → recovery. FIXED 2026-06-25 (snxtrans.c + snxdef.h): added `SnxTransTcpRecvN` (recv EXACTLY n bytes, poll(POLLIN) on EAGAIN); rewrote `SnxTransTcpRcvPacket` to read the 20-byte header, parse payload_len via `SnxCodeGet4ByteData` (offset 16, byte order from flags byte offset 2), then read exactly payload → returns one complete PDU (no over/under-read). Rewrote `SnxTransTcpTxPacket` to loop send() until the whole PDU is written, poll(POLLOUT) on EAGAIN. New snxdef.h consts SNX_AGENTX_HDR_FLAGS_OFFSET=2 / _PAYLOADLEN_OFFSET=16 / SNX_TRANS_POLL_TIMEOUT_MS=1000; `#include <poll.h>`. BONUS: old send-fail path did `SelAddWrFd → SnxTransTcpOutSocket → SNX_TRANS_RDY_EVT → SnxMainOpenSession`, i.e. every backpressure partial-send reopened the AgentX session (session churn under load) — now gone. Tradeoff: one PDU per read event (the SNX_MUL_REQ_PKT batch loop in SnxMainProcessRcvdPkt is now never hit but harmless); add batching later if throughput needs it. Still to verify on DUT: rapid snmpbulkwalk/snmpget storm on ifTable/ifXTable keeps 705 ESTABLISHED (no manual disable/enable). Secondary contributor (not addressed): master `agentXTimeout 5`/`agentXRetries 1` under single-SNMP-task saturation.

**DESIGN PIVOT (2026-06-30, design review): Plan C now goes with Option B** — spec at `~/plan-c-agentx-owned-getset-split-design-2026-06-30.md`. Supersedes "change A (hardcode skip ifmibdb) + Q2 (ISS-side SET up-call)". Three parts: (1) **agentx_owned.list delegation whitelist** (per 6/2 docx `~/SNMP_Plan_C_Design_2026-06-02.docx`): `ies_auto_mibs.c` reads `/etc/moxa/netsnmp/agentx_owned.list` (default `ifmibdb/`), skips local `netsnmp_register_*` ONLY for RO entries whose URI prefix matches → master longest-prefix-routes RO ifTable/ifXTable GET to ISS subagent; RW (ifAdminStatus) stays local → SET via framework. Replaces change A's full-ifmibdb-skip with per-RO-column skip; restore the `MOX_SNMP_INIT_ENTRY(ifmibdb_MibEntry)` to normal registration. (2) **Revert Q2** (`ifmibwr.c` PortSetAdminStatus2MxCfgAsync) — SET back on framework, no ISS up-call. (3) **VACM exposure whitelist** on master: replace `view all included .1` with curated `view included` derived from `ies_auto_mibs_setup.c` MOX_SNMP_INIT_ENTRY list (+8691 enterprise, +ifTable .2/ifXTable .31, +system .1/snmp .11/SNMPv3 .1.3.6.1.6.3) → hides ISS-leaked extras (VRRP 68/MAU 26/etc.), so the `excluded .68` band-aid becomes redundant. Rationale incl. layering: agentx_owned.list keeps SET in middleware (top-down, no ISS up-call); net-snmp master treats AgentX subagent and dlmod handler uniformly (verified `agentx/master.c:466/617` `agentx_master_handler`→`snmp_pdu_create(AGENTX_MSG_*)`→`snmp_async_send`; `master_admin.c:223` registers handler bound to subagent session). Note: net-snmp here compiles NO ip/tcp/udp/icmp modules (only ies_auto_mibs/dlmod/proxy/snmp_mib/system_mib/sysORTable/SNMPv3 — `mib_module_inits.h`), so all standard MIB-2 comes from ISS subagent + ies_auto_mibs, NOT net-snmp host modules. Status: spec + plan written (`~/plan-c-agentx-owned-getset-split-{design,PLAN}-2026-06-30.md`); **all code tasks IMPLEMENTED 2026-06-30, awaiting build + DUT verify**. Files changed: `plugin_moxa_snmp/app/script/agentx_owned.list` (new, `ifmibdb/`) + `plugin_moxa_snmp/Makefile` (install → /etc/moxa/netsnmp/); `ies-auto-mibs/ies_auto_mibs.c` (reader `mox_snmp_load_agentx_owned_list` + `mox_snmp_entry_is_agentx_owned` using `entry->mode & HANDLER_CAN_SET` for RW-detect + `entry->uri` prefix; skip in `mox_snmp_init_entry` loop before GenerateTableIndexEntry, `free(entry);continue;`); `ies_auto_mibs_setup.c` (restored `MOX_SNMP_INIT_ENTRY(ifmibdb_MibEntry)`); `config_moxa_snmp_control.c` (VACM blacklist, kept `included .1`, 16 excludes ×2 blocks); `cfa2/src/ifmibwr.c` (reverted Q2). Build: `make plugin_moxa_snmp-rebuild 3rdparty_net_snmp-rebuild app_moxa_iss_10_1_0-rebuild && make`.

**ifAdminStatus GET-forward (2026-07-01, implemented):** Option B's RO/RW split alone does NOT fix ifTable walk perf — proven via pcap `~/pcap/2026-07-01_snmp-agentx_owned.list-*.pcapng`: every multi-varbind ifTable GETNEXT (frames 7/8, 92/93, 178/180, 266/267) took a constant ~636ms because the bundle includes ifAdminStatus (2.2.1.7, RW) which stays on framework → slow `entry_handle_generate_iss_value_file`/ies_uri_handle path drags the whole PDU (RO varbinds go to ISS fast; the one RW varbind poisons the response). Fix: in `ies_auto_mibs.c` `mox_snmp_handle_entry` GET branch, when entry is ifAdminStatus (OID `{1,3,6,1,2,1,2,2,1,7}`, oid_len 10), forward the GET to the ISS AgentX subagent and return; SET/SET_COMMIT branch untouched (SET stays framework → layering clean). Mechanism: `netsnmp_subtree_find(ifIndex probe OID 1.3.6.1.2.1.2.2.1.1.1)` (RO, ISS-owned/not-shadowed, and ISS registers the whole interfaces group 1.3.6.1.2.1.2 as ONE region per snxmain.c:870 SnxMainRegisterMibs so it covers ifAdminStatus) → `netsnmp_call_handlers(iss_sub->reginfo, reqinfo, request)`. This EXACT pattern already exists in the file (entry_handle_exception, line ~1867). agentx_master_handler is async/delegated (master.c:448 session=handler->myvoid set at master_admin.c:232; master.c:590 REQUEST_IS_DELEGATED), so forward+return integrates with net-snmp's delegated flow (value filled when ISS replies). ISS down → subtree_find fails → falls through to slow local path (graceful). Two new static helpers `mox_snmp_entry_is_ifadminstatus` + `mox_snmp_forward_get_to_iss` before mox_snmp_handle_entry. Awaiting build+DUT verify. This is the GET-fast + SET-clean resolution to the "AgentX routes whole OID" tension (splits GET/SET at the framework handler, not at registration).

**CORRECTED understanding of the OID surface (2026-06-30, verified):** earlier "ISS leaks its whole tree → need whitelist" was WRONG. ies_auto_mibs_setup.c actually registers ~66 DBs (column-level depth ~11) covering nearly all standard+enterprise MIBs incl ip(`net_stdipdb.h` has 4.22 ARP), **VRRP `net_vrrpdb.h` registers 1.3.6.1.2.1.68**, ospf, bridge, mau?no — so it FULLY shadows ISS for those. **The VRRP(68.1.1.0) badValue walk-truncation is a FRAMEWORK vrrpdb handler bug (present in mainline too — mainline walk also truncates at 68.1.1.0), NOT an ISS leak.** The only REAL ISS leak = standard groups framework registers 0 of: tcp(6), rip(23), mau(26), entity(47), std-radius(67), plus ISS-native 83/85/97/185/241, plus the new sub-tables icmp 5.29/5.30 & udp 7.7/7.8/7.9 (framework covers icmp 5.1-5.26 / udp 7.1-7.5). Hence Option B's exposure curation is a 16-entry BLACKLIST (not whitelist): exclude those leaked groups + mask 68. mainline walk (`~/snmp-mainline-2026_0609_1932`) is itself truncated at 68 so NOT a usable baseline. default `snmpwalk` (no OID) walks mib-2 only; enterprise 8691 is a separate walk and is clean. TODO (separate from Plan C): fix framework vrrpdb handler so VRRP-MIB works (it breaks mainline mib-2 walks for all customers).

